          #EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(-) \colon CartSp \longrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              which sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              to (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of) its
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              In other words, for two
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and the algebra homomorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ←
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(X)\leftarrow C^\infty(Y)
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds+into+formal+duals+of+R-algebras"} embedding of smooth manifolds into formal duals of R-algebras
            for more on this.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              One has to be careful that prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
              might seem to imply more than it does. In order that all constructions on all commutative algebras have the desired dual effect on formally dual smooth spaces (e.g. construction of
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/products"} products
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+differentials"} Kähler differentials
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+algebras"} smooth algebras
          %p
            Now to pass to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superalgebra"} superalgebra
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              It is an observation from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
              (from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stern-Gerlach+experiment"} Stern-Gerlach experiment
              via the
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-statistics+theorem"} spin-statistics theorem
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+fields"} physical fields
              for
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+theories"} physical theories
              that contain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
              behave as if they have
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
              which are not quite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
              only commute with each other up to picking up a minus sign.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-commutative+superalgebra"} super-commutative superalgebra
              (or just
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+superalgebra"} commutative superalgebra
              for short) is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+algebra"} graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi even
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi odd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = A_{even} \oplus A_{odd}
              such that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a,b
              any two elements in homogeneous degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi deg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi deg
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} deg(a), deg(b)\in \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ausdehnungslehre"} Grassmann 1844, §37, §55
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi deg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    a \cdot b = (-1)^{deg(a) deg(b)} b \cdot a
                    \\,.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi SuperCAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperCAlg_{\mathbb{R}}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of commutative superalgebras over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
          #SuperCartesianSpace.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|q})
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\wedge^\bullet \langle \theta^1, \cdots, \theta^q\rangle
            %p
              is the
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} freely
              generated from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta^i\}_{i = 1}^q
              subject to the relation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta^i \theta^j = - \theta^j \theta^i
                    \\,.
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi q
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,q \in \mathbb{N}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Cartesian+space"} super-Cartesian space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the commutative superalgebra written
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{p|q})
              whose underlying
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2\mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℝ
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{p|q})
                    \\coloneqq
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^p) \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \wedge^\bullet\langle\theta^1, \cdots, \theta^q\rangle
            %p with the product given by the relations
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi f
                              %msup
                                %mi θ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msup
                                %mi θ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi i
                                    %mi k
                              %mo )
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mi g
                              %msup
                                %mi θ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi j
                                    %mn 1
                              %mi ⋯
                              %msup
                                %mi θ
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi j
                                    %mi l
                              %mo )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi f
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi g
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi k
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi l
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mi l
                            %mi g
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi f
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi j
                                  %mi l
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi ⋯
                            %msup
                              %mi θ
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi i
                                  %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\left(
                    f \theta^{i_1}\cdots \theta^{i_k}
                    \\right)
                    \\left(
                    g \theta^{j_1}\cdots \theta^{j_l}
                    \\right)
                    \&amp; =
                    f \cdot g \; \theta^{i_1}\cdots \theta^{i_k} \theta^{j_1}\cdots \theta^{j_l}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    (-1)^{k l} g\cdot f \; \theta^{j_1}\cdots \theta^{j_l} \theta^{i_1}\cdots \theta^{i_k}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \cdot g
              is the ordinary pointwise product of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperCartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi SuperCAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SuperCartSp \hookrightarrow SuperCAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+superalgebras"} commutative superalgebras
              on those of this form. We write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SuperCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q} \in SuperCartSp
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{p|q})
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Say that a collection of morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperCartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperCartSp
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covering"} covering
              if all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
              and the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q}
              (for the same
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              and
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\theta_i\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/good+open+cover"} good open cover
              in the sense of def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SiteCartSp"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi SuperCartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SuperSmooth0Type \coloneqq Sh(SuperCartSp)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              over that site. We call this the collection of
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+spaces"} smooth super spaces
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            that hosts traditional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+supergeometry"} synthetic differential supergeometry
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_6 Remark
            %p
              The even-degree part
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi even
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{p|q})_{even}
              is an ordinary
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \geq 1
              then it is not the algebra of functions on any
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
              may be thought of as a function depending on an
              = succeed "." do
                %em infinitesimal direction
            %p
              For instance
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi even
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^{0|2})_{even}
              is isomorphic to what is known as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+dual+numbers"} algebra of dual numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}\oplus \epsilon \mathbb{R})/(\epsilon^2)
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mn 1
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon = \theta^1 \theta^2
            %p
              This is traditionally more familiar from the theory of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+schemes"} formal schemes
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            %p
              But this means that in passing to commutative superalgebras there are
              %em two
              stages of generalizations of plain differential geometry involved:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
                  are generalized to
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+manifolds"} formal smooth manifolds
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+smooth+manifolds"} formal smooth manifolds
                  are further generalized to formal smooth
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
          %p It will be useful to make this explicit.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    InfPoint \hookrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebras"} commutative algebras
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}\oplus V
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              a finite-dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"} infinitesimally thickened points
            %p Write moreover
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CartSp \rtimes InfPoint \hookrightarrow CAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of those algebras which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
              of commutative
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \otimes C^\infty(D)
            %p
              of algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^p)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              as in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EmbeddingOfSmoothManifoldsIntoFormalDualsOfRAlgebras"}
              with algebras corresponding to infinitesimally thickened points
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              as above.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FormalSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    FormalSmooth0Type \coloneqq Sh(CartSp \rtimes InfPoint)
            %p
              is traditionally known as the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cahiers+topos"} Cahiers topos
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+dual+numbers"} algebra of dual numbers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}\longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              which are the identity after restriction along
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝔻
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^n \times \mathbb{D}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ϵ
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟵
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n) \oplus \epsilon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n))
                    \\longleftarrow
                    C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
            %p
              which are the identity modulo
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϵ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f + (\partial f) \epsilon
            %p
              for some smooth function
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\partial f) \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_1,f_2 \in C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (f_1 f_2 + (\partial (f_1 f_2))\epsilon )
                    \=
                    (f_1 + (\partial f_1) \epsilon)
                    (f_2 + (\partial f_2) \epsilon)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Multiplying this out and using that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon^2 = 0
              this in turn is equivalent to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo ∂
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\partial(f_1 f_2) = (\partial f_1) f_2 + f_1 (\partial f_2)
                    \\,.
            %p
              This in turn means equivalently that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial\colon C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)\to C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              are equivalent to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+fields"} vector fields
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations+of+smooth+functions+are+vector+fields"} derivations of smooth functions are vector fields
            %p In particular one finds that maps
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔻
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{D} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^n
            %p
              are equivalently single
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+vectors"} tangent vectors
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperInfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi SuperCAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SuperInfPoint \hookrightarrow SuperCAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on those
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+superalgebras"} commutative superalgebras
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
              on those of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}\oplus V
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              a finite dimensional
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+ideal"} nilpotent ideal
            %p
              We call this the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoints"} superpoints
            %p Similarly write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi SuperInfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %msubsup
                      %mi SuperCAlg
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CartSp \rtimes SuperInfPoint
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    SuperCAlg_{\mathbb{R}}^{op}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+products"} tensor products
              of an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
              and an algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(D)
              on an infinitesimally thickened superpoint.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SuperSmooth
                    %mn 0
                    %mi Type
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi SuperInfPoint
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    SuperSmooth0Type \coloneqq Sh(CartSp \rtimes SuperInfPoint)
            %p
              we call that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+smooth+infinity-groupoid"} super formal smooth spaces
          %h4#TheGeometricDeterminations The geometric determinations
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
            considered above are related by a sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflections
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflections
            as follows
          #InclusionOfSites.num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi InfPoint
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi SuperInfPoint
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\ast \hookrightarrow CartSp
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    CartSp\rtimes InfPoint
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    CartSp \rtimes SuperInfPoint
            %p
              for the evident
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+inclusions"} full inclusions
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the first one picks the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^0
              %li
                %p
                  the second one regards
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                  as a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+manifold"} formal manifold
                  equipped with no infinitesimal thickening;
              %li
                %p
                  the third one regards
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mi n
                        %mo ×
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n \times D
                  as a supergeometric space with no odd-graded (no fermionic) component.
          #SequenceOfSites.num_remark
            %h6#remark_7 Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sites"} sites
              in question are alternatingly (co-)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
              of each other (we always display
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints"} left adjoints
              above their right adjoints)
