                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⇝
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightsquigarrow
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic modality
                  and whose left piece
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⇉
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightrightarrows
                  produces
                  %em super-even
                  components, containing all the “
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
                  = succeed "\u201D" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+currents"} conserved currents
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unity+of+opposites"} unity of opposites
                  hence deserves to be called the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermionic+modality"} fermionic modality
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  is the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rheonomy+modality"} rheonomy modality
            %p
              Hence we get a progression of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+modalities"} adjoint modalities
