          %h4#PrincipalBundlesAndHigherGeometry Principal bundles and Higher geometry
          %p
            The point of the system of modalities in corollary
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfModalities"}
            is that they allow to carry various geometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory"} theory
            across different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
            of geometry. If we formulate traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FormalSmooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FormalSmooth0Type
            with just these operations, then we may just carry that verbatim to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperFormalSmooth
                  %mn 0
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalSmooth0Type
            to get a theory of super-Cartan geometry. This we get to below.
          %p
            In the same vein, we may increase the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SuperFormalSmooth
                  %mi n
                  %mi Type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SuperFormalSmooth n Type
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 0
            and get
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Cartan+geometry"} higher Cartan geometry
          %p
            In fact at least
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            is necessary in order to formalize
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundles"} frame bundles
            via their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modulating+morphisms"} modulating morphisms
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}GL(V)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            is obtained by replacing in the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stacks"} stacks
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \infty
            is obtained by further refining this to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stacks"} infinity-stacks
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"} infinity-groupoids
          %p
            Here we just recall some bare minimum of this
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame+bundles"} frame bundles
            and hence here we mainly need the concept of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} principal infinity-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+principal+bundles"} geometry of physics – principal bundles
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analogy"} analog
              of prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoReflectionsOfToposes"}
              still holds, and produces via the direct analog corollary
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfModalities"}
              a system of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operators"} modal operators
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SuperFormalSmooth%E2%88%9EType"} SuperFormalSmooth∞Type
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+object"} group object
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"}> ∞-group
              ), the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} principal bundles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
              on any
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are equivalent to morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}G
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              object of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    P &amp;\longrightarrow &amp; \ast
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                    }
                    \\,.
          %h3#GStructureAndCartanGeometry
            %strong 2)
            General Cartan geometry
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohesion"} differential cohesion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            as in corollary
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SystemOfModalities"}
            above (hence an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elastic"} elastic
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/substance"} substance
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifolds"} V-manifolds
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structures"} G-structures
            on these. Applied to the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometry
            as established in prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CoReflectionsOfToposes"}
            this hence yields a theory of
            = succeed "-structures" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"} V-manifold
            in supergeometry, and hence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            modeled on the inclusion
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⋊
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \to G \rtimes V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abstract+general"} abstract general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            formulated axiomatically this way. Below in
            %em
              %a{:href => "#SuperCartanGeometry"} Super Cartan geometry
            we then specify to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+particular"} concrete particular
            super Cartan geometry.
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#Manifolds"} V-Manifolds
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#FrameBundles"} Frame bundles
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#GStructure"} G-Structure
          %h4#Manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            \-Manifolds
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+manifolds+and+orbifolds"} geometry of physics – manifolds and orbifolds
          #LocalDiffeomorphisms.num_defn
            %h6#definition_11 Definition
            %p
              Given
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y\in \mathbf{H}
              then a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X\longrightarrow Y
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              if its naturality square of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+shape+modality"} infinitesimal shape modality
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              square.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_10 Remark
            %p
              The abstract definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              comes down to being the appropriate
              = succeed "-version" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+supergeometry"} synthetic differential supergeometry
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              if the diagram of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundles"} tangent bundles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi T
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi T
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    T X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{T f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}}
                    \\\
                    T Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Y
                    }
            %p
              To see this, notice by the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
              that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,X]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/jet+bundle"} jet bundle
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with jets of order as encoded by the infinitesimal order of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^1(1)
              is the first order infinitesimal interval defined by the fact that its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of functions
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+dual+numbers"} algebra of dual numbers
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(\mathbb{D}^1(1)) = (\mathbb{R} \oplus \epsilon \mathbb{R})/(\epsilon^2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\mathbb{D}^1(1), X]\simeq T X
            %p
              is the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [D,-]
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              in its second argument, and that, by the hom-adjunction,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(U, [D,X]) \simeq \mathbf{H}(U \times D, X)
              and finally use that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ×
                      %mi D
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℜ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ×
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(U \times D, \Im X)\simeq \mathbf{H}(\Re(U \times D), X)\simeq \mathbf{H}(U,X)
          %p
            Let now
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \in \mathbf{H}
            be given, equipped with the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"}> infinity-group
            ).
          #VManifold.num_defn
            %h6#definition_12 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V-manifold"} V-manifold
              is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathbf{H}
              such that there exists a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondence"} correspondence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mi et
                            %mo ↙
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi et
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \&amp;&amp; U
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{et}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{et}}
                    \\\
                    V &amp;&amp; &amp;&amp; X
                    }
            %p
              with both morphisms being
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphisms"} local diffeomorphisms
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphism"} epimorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atlas"} atlas
          #BosonicModalityPreservesLocalDiffeomorphism.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_7 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; X \longrightarrow Y
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocalDiffeomorphisms"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi f
                      %mo ⇝
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⇝
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mover
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ⇝
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{f}\colon \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{X} \longrightarrow \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{Y}
              under the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic modality
          .proof
            %h6#proof_4 Proof
            %p
              Since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+modality"} bosonic modality
              provides
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aufhebung"} Aufhebung
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℜ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Re\dashv \Im
              by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Sublations"}
              we have
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⇝
                      %mi ℑ
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℑ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightsquigarrow \Im \simeq \Im
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℑ
                    %mo ⇝
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℑ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Im \rightsquigarrow \simeq \Im
              anyway. Finally
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇝
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightsquigarrow
              preserves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
              (being in particular a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi X
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Y
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im X
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{f}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im f}}
                    \\\
                    Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im Y
                    }
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇝
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rightsquigarrow\;\;
              yields a pullback diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⇝
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mover
                              %mi X
                              %mo ⇝
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ⇝
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ℑ
                                  %mover
                                    %mi f
                                    %mo ⇝
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ⇝
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi ℑ
                            %mover
                              %mi Y
                              %mo ⇝
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{X} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{X}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{f}}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\Im \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{f}}}
                    \\\
                    \\stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{Y} &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; \Im \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{Y}
                    }
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary_2 Corollary
            %p
              The bosonic space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ⇝
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{X}
              underlying a
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#VManifold"}
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⇝
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \stackrel{\rightsquigarrow}{V}
          %h4#FrameBundles Frame bundles
          #GeneralLinearGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_13 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+infinity-group"} automorphism infinity-group
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mi e
                        %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{D}^V_e
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InfinitesimalDiskBundle"}
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %msubsup
                        %mi 𝔻
                        %mi e
                        %mi V
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \colon \ast \to \mathbb{D}^V_e \to V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝔻
                      %mi e
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    GL(V) \coloneqq \mathbf{Aut}(\mathbb{D}^V_e)
