                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion"} torsion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{siso})
              which have “all indices contracted”. (See also at
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+constraints+in+supergravity"} torsion constraints in supergravity
            %p Notably we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi d
