              %h3#the_brane_molecule The Brane molecule
              %p
                Furthermore, there exists a more general classification of possible supermembranes in spacetime with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
                spatial dimensions and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                time dimensions, appearing in (
                %a{:href => "#BlencoweDuff88"}> Blencowe-Duff 88
                ). In this sense, the brane scan is but the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T=1
                branch of the brane molecule. The objects appearing here are expected to be related to other generalizations of string theory. See
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D12+supergravity"} D=12 supergravity
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+M-theory"} bosonic M-theory
              %p
                %img{:alt => "The brane molecule without assuming super Poincare invariance.", :src => "/nlab/files/branemoleculepc.png"}/
              %p Compare:
              %ul
                %li#BlencoweDuff88
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Miles+Blencowe"}> Miles Blencowe
                    ,
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Duff"} Mike Duff
                    = succeed "," do
                      %em Supermembranes and the Signature of Space-time
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a{:href => "inspirehep.net/record/262142"} spire:262142
                    = succeed "," do
                      %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(88)90155-1"} 10.1016/0550-3213(88)90155-1
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/262142/files/cer-000099708.pdf"} pdf
                %li
                  %p
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
          %h4#DefiniteSuperForms Definite super-forms
          %p
            A rich source of traditional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
            comes from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+holonomy"} special holonomy
            induced by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+forms"} definite forms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            as discussed above.
          %p First consider the traditional situation
          #DefiniteForm.num_defn
            %h6#definition_26 Definition
            %p
              Consider a real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              and a form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \wedge^{p+2} V^\ast
              regarded as a constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \Omega^{p+2}(V)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              Consider then a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo =
                      %mi dim
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = dim(V)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+form"} differential form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^{p+2}(X)
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite form
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              if its restriction to each
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+space"} tangent space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi x
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_x X \simeq V
              is in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit"} orbit
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              under the natural
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback+of+differential+forms"} pullback of differential forms
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_15 Proposition
            %p
              A choice of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+form"} definite form
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefiniteForm"}
              = succeed "-manifold" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              is equivalent to a choice of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Stab
                      %mrow
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = Stab_{GL(V)}(\phi) \hookrightarrow GL(V)
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi GL
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(V)
          .num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                        %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{R}^{2n}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              the canonical
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+group"} symplectic group
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
              in this case is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/almost+symplectic+structure"} almost symplectic structure
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \mathbb{R}^7
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+3-form"} associative 3-form
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+group"} stabilizer group
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82"} G₂
              and a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-structure"} G-structure
              in this case is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G%E2%82%82-structure"} G₂-structure
          %p
            Now the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mover
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo ∧
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ⋯
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi p
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = \overline{\psi} \wedge E^{a_1} \wedge \cdots E^{a_p}\wedge \psi
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            serve as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            forms for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super+p-brane"} Green-Schwarz super p-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            on super-Minkowki spacetime. The globalization of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma+models"} sigma models
            to curved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetimes"} superspacetimes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            requires, in particular, that these
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            are extended as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definite+forms"} definite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .num_example
            %h6#side_remark Side Remark
            %p
              This is discussed further at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "Green-Schwarz+action+functional#OnCurvedSpacetime"} Green-Schwarz action functional – On curved target spacetime
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
              is a higher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Super+Gerbes"} Super Gerbes
              which is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+prequantization"} higher prequantization
              of this cocycle, and hence its definition requires the lift of the definite cocycle form to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+model"} parameterized WZW model
              over superspacetime. Discussion of this
              = succeed "-cancellation" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+anomaly"} classical anomaly
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
              on curved supergravity targets is the content at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Cartan+Geometry"} Higher Cartan Geometry
          %p
            Since the cocycles in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            are not just closed forms, but are also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} cocycles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            under the action of the whole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"}> Lie bracket
            , i.e. to ask for stabilization both of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            form as well as the bracket.
          #StabilizerOfSupersymmetryJointWith3Cocycle.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_16 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1,N}
              be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 4
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 6
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 10
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in \{3,4,6,10\}
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in \Omega^{3}(\mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|N})
              the corresponding 3-form characterizing the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-brane"} super-1-brane
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"}> superstring
              ) in this dimension, according to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
              \. Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
              of both the super Lie bracket and the cocycle is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin group
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
